$\begin{align}
\text{vertex's }r\text{-coordinate}&=\dfrac{(\goldD{-11})+(\goldD{-14})}{2}
\\\\
&=\blueD{-\dfrac{25}{2}}
\end{align}$

Now we can find the vertex's $y$-coordinate by evaluating $g\left(\blueD{-\dfrac{25}{2}}\right)$:

$\begin{align}
g\left(\blueD{-\dfrac{25}{2}}\right)&=-\left(\blueD{-\dfrac{25}{2}}+11\right)\left(\blueD{-\dfrac{25}{2}}+14\right)
\\\\
&=-\left(-\dfrac32\right)\left(\dfrac32\right)
\\\\
&=\dfrac{9}{4}
\end{align}$
